Emilli Remote for Windows, branch windows-153
=============================================

This branch is the complete corresponding source of the Windows program that
Emilli Remote Setup (branch easy-windows) installs: RustDesk 1.5.3 for
Windows x64, built by LoomNaru Labs Inc with the workflow
.github/workflows/build-windows-emilli.yml. It is a modified version of
RustDesk, the open source remote desktop software by Purslane Tech Pte. Ltd.
and the RustDesk contributors (https://github.com/rustdesk/rustdesk).
RustDesk is licensed under the GNU Affero General Public License, version 3
(AGPL-3.0); see the file LICENCE. This modified version is distributed under
the same licence, without any warranty.

Base: RustDesk tag 1.5.3, commit 95cca3f661f635b3cc85c04935fe8d96d8f432ef,
with libs/hbb_common at commit fae47e024dd83cef6aaecde0aa7d11731df11649
included as plain files (the import commit, whose parent is the 1.5.0
import shared with main and android-play), then upstream's workflows
removed. The same changes on 1.5.0 are on branch windows-emilli.

Changes, each in its own commit:

1. res/icon.ico, res/tray-icon.ico, flutter/windows/runner/resources/app_icon.ico,
   flutter/assets/icon.svg: the Emilli Remote icon for the program, its window,
   taskbar, shortcuts, tray and the in-app icon.
2. src/common.rs: the program never asks RustDesk's servers for a new version,
   so it shows no update notice and never updates itself to the official
   RustDesk build.
3. flutter/lib/common.dart, src/tray.rs, src/platform/windows.rs: "Emilli
   Remote" is the name shown in the title bar, the tray tooltip and Programs
   and Features (publisher LoomNaru Labs Inc). The internal name stays
   "RustDesk": install folder, settings folders, service, pipes, registry key,
   shortcut file names and server settings are unchanged.
4. .github/workflows/build-windows-emilli.yml, NOTICE, .github/README.md: the
   build, following upstream's own Windows job at tag 1.5.3.

"RustDesk" is the name of the upstream project. This build is not made,
endorsed or supported by the RustDesk developers. For the official RustDesk
apps, go to https://rustdesk.com or https://github.com/rustdesk/rustdesk.

Branch easy3-windows (brief REMOTE-EASY-3), on top of windows-153-ui:

5. libs/hbb_common/src/config.rs, src/lang.rs, src/platform/windows.rs,
   src/core_main.rs, src/flutter.rs, src/auth_2fa.rs, flutter/windows/runner/Runner.rc,
   Cargo.toml, flutter/lib/common.dart, flutter/lib/desktop/widgets/tabbar_widget.dart,
   flutter/lib/desktop/pages/desktop_setting_page.dart: one name everywhere. The
   internal app name is "EmilliRemote" (install folder, settings folders, service,
   pipes, registry keys; no spaces, for Windows service and command lines); the
   name people see is "Emilli Remote" (translations, window titles, service display
   name, shortcuts, Start menu folder, start-up shortcut, toasts, the 2FA label, the
   program's file properties). No "powered by" line; About links to this repository.
   Server settings are never read from the program's file name.
6. src/emilli.rs, src/client.rs, src/server/connection.rs, src/hbbs_http/sync.rs,
   libs/base/protos/message.proto (LoginRequest field 101): PCs signed in to the same
   account open each other without the PC's own password. The controller asks the
   account server for a one-time ticket bound to the connection's challenge; the PC
   being opened asks the account server to confirm it. Per-PC switch
   emilli-account-access (direct, click, off) in Settings > Security, sent with the
   heartbeat. Test seam EMILLI_REMOTE_INSTANCE (a second copy with its own settings
   on one Windows machine, for CI).
7. flutter/lib/common/widgets/emilli_account.dart, flutter/lib/desktop/pages/connection_page.dart,
   flutter/lib/models/peer_tab_model.dart, src/lang/en.rs, src/lang/ko.rs: before
   sign-in the first screen shows "가입" and "로그인" (sign-up inside the app with an
   invite link or the sign-up code); after sign-in only "내 기기" (the account's
   devices); Settings > Account has "이 PC를 내 계정에서 빼기"; the ID server's
   refusals and the account server's messages are plain sentences.
   flutter/lib/common/widgets/peer_card.dart: one click on a device opens it on
   desktop too (a double-click still opens it once).
8. src/emilli.rs, src/hbbs_http/sync.rs, src/flutter_ffi.rs, flutter/lib/models/user_model.dart,
   flutter/lib/models/group_model.dart, flutter/lib/common/widgets/emilli_account.dart: binding this
   PC to an account, taking it out and saving its switch on the account server are signed with the
   key this PC registered with the ID server (a server nonce, Ed25519); signing in alone binds
   nothing. A sign-in the server ended (password changed) is said on the first screen.
